l_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98656","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This multiplies light energy by the specified factor, but only when shadows are enabled **and** when using the Compatibility rendering method.\r\n\r\nThis can be decreased below 1.0 to compensate for lights having a different brightness due to sRGB blending being used for those lights.\r\n\r\nThis feature makes it easier to [adapt projects to the web platform when you also want them to run on native platforms](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/pull/1127), while still using Forward+/Mobile on native platforms. It also benefits projects that want to make full use of the automatic fallback to Compatibility.\r\n\r\n- See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/90259\r\nand https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10824.\r\n\r\n## Preview\r\n\r\n*Using a **Shadow Light Energy Compatibility** value of `0.3333` on all examples.*\r\n\r\n### Positional shadows\r\n\r\n*Lights at the top always have shadows disabled for comparison.*\r\n\r\nShadows disabled | Shadows enabled\r\n-|-\r\n![shadows_off](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f453a1e5-956e-4fc2-9df8-3e40a6253aa0) | ![shadows_on](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c987e808-984b-4f07-9c25-b3920cc88c8e)\r\n\r\n### Directional shadow\r\n\r\nShadows disabled | Shadows enabled\r\n-|-\r\n![directional_shadows_off](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2cc6f167-f712-4ca5-a74a-2502247907cd) | ![directional_shadows_on](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1fd2bd9-415a-4817-9b84-21f8779e86ab)\r\n\r\n## TODO\r\n\r\n- [ ] Lower default value for the preview DirectionalLight3D that's used in the editor. Be conservative, but it should definitely be less than 0.5 (probably around 